why: the note opens on an actor the site does not name and uses a name the reader cannot place; Kirill on 2026-09-21: "This looks out of blue and hard to follow"; the fix that day was a rule putting the site's subject first, and the rule of 2026-09-21 reverses it so the fact keeps its own subject, which is what the barred wording is here for: the fact's own subject is the outside thing the fact is about, and a chooser the code never names is not one; the expected form places the outside name with an appositive, and no check reaches this, so judgement decides it
